"""Human US-unit report derived from tail_analysis.json and mass_properties.json."""
from parameters import *
from display_units import length,mass,volume,inch

def section(a,m,c):
    def table(head,rows):
        return '| '+' | '.join(head)+' |\n| '+' | '.join('---' for _ in head)+' |\n'+''.join('| '+' | '.join(map(str,row))+' |\n' for row in rows)
    text='## Tail fins, pressure estimate and flat carriage\n\n'
    import math
    width=2*(FIN_TIP_R*math.cos(math.radians(FIN_ANGLES[0]))+FIN_T/2*math.sin(math.radians(FIN_ANGLES[0])))
    text+=f"Four identical trapezoidal PETG fins sit at 50, 130, 230 and 310 degrees around the rod on two separate slotted collars. The 80/100 degree spacing tilts them closer to vertical so a descending fin clears the next dart's microphone rain hood. Each fin has a {length(FIN_X1-FIN_X0)} root chord, {length(FIN_TIP_X1-FIN_TIP_X0)} tip chord, {length(FIN_TIP_R-FIN_ROOT_R)} exposed radial span and {length(FIN_T,3)} thickness. Its root runs from {length(FIN_X0)} to {length(FIN_X1)} from the tip. Maximum radius from the rod axis is {length(FIN_TIP_R)}; the diagonal orientation limits carried width to about {length(width)}. Four fins add side area in both pitch and yaw.\n\n"
    text+=f"The two collars begin at {length(FIN_COLLARS[0])} and {length(FIN_COLLARS[1])} from the tip, each {length(FIN_COLLAR_L)} long, with {length(2*FIN_COLLAR_R)} OD and a {length(FIN_BORE_D,3)} bore. Two tabs per fin seat in open axial keyways with {length(FIN_SLOT_T-FIN_T,3)} total thickness clearance and {length(.4,3)} total axial clearance. The fins print on their full broad face; the collars print on an axial end face with vertical bore/keyways. Both need no supports. PETG is solid at the existing profile.\n\n"
    text+=f"Install the collars and four fins before the pod. Dry-fit all eight tabs; align the open wire reliefs on the cell-wire side and keep them free of adhesive. Bond both collar bores and all fin tabs using a PETG-compatible adhesive verified by a coupon. Roughen/clean the rod locally and hold the panel angles while curing. The mass model includes {mass(M.fin_adhesive_mass)} total cured adhesive as a MEASURE allowance; the CAD bond films are representative, not exact fillets. Weigh the actual cured build, and use the same joints and fins on the dummy. Joint strength, fin stiffness and long-term creep are untested. Do not rely on a loose sliding collar or on keyway friction. Service requires debonding; the exploded layout identifies the pieces without claiming a reversible dry assembly.\n\n"
    text+='The fin tips stay inside the available dart spacing. This trades away the span of a larger lawn-dart tail: the long chord supplies area while the diagonal panels preserve clearance. No fin, collar or pod scaling is used during release. The tail already sits below and beyond the deck; it does not need to pass through the head slots. Only the head and post cross those gaps. Full-size geometry is included in carried, mid-release, vertical extraction, later prescribed pitch, stood, dummy and web assemblies. The microphone corridor, removable USB cap and complete antenna strip remain unobstructed. This is a span-constrained prototype, not an optimized aerodynamic design.\n\n'
    gap=next(r for r in c['checks'] if r['check']=='tail_to_neighbor_pod_extraction')
    text+=f"The limiting sampled fin-to-neighbour-pod gap is **{length(gap['min_clearance_mm'],3)}**, measured by true B-rep closest distance, at **{length(gap['worst_dart_drop_neighbor'][1],3)} downward extraction** of dart {gap['worst_dart_drop_neighbor'][0]} beside dart {gap['worst_dart_drop_neighbor'][2]}. This is nominal CAD separation, not a tolerance or flex guarantee.\n\n"
    text+='The pressure calculation uses uniform pressure on the union of the actual projected side silhouettes: **CP = sum(projected area x area-centroid distance) / sum(projected area)**. Rod, body including cell, pod, antenna strip/backer, fins and collars are projected onto the longitudinal/transverse plane; occupied pixels remove hidden rod and overlapping fin area. This is a cardboard-cutout estimate. It does not assign validated small-angle force coefficients. `tail_analysis.py` repeats rolls from 0 through 165 degrees in 15 degree steps and halves the raster pitch at each sampled worst case. `out/tail_analysis.json` retains all component areas and centroid distances, both geometries/masses and convergence results.\n\n'
    text+=f"Aim: at least **{a['target_minimum_body_widths']:.0f} body widths** behind the CG at the sampled worst roll, to give a visible geometric restoring lever despite uncertainty. One body width means the cradle/gutter breadth **{length(a['body_width_mm'],3)}**; it excludes the tall hanger. This is a design screen, not a standard or a demonstrated fall-stability requirement. The same denominator is used before and after.\n\n"
    text+=table(['Model estimate','Before fins','With fins'],[
        ('Dart mass',mass(a['before']['mass_g']),mass(a['after']['mass_g'])),
        ('CG from tip',length(a['before']['cg_mm'][0],3),length(a['after']['cg_mm'][0],3)),
        ('CP from tip, sampled minimum margin',length(a['before']['minimum']['cp_x_mm'],3),length(a['after']['minimum']['cp_x_mm'],3)),
        ('Static margin, sampled minimum',length(a['before']['minimum']['static_margin_mm'],3),length(a['after']['minimum']['static_margin_mm'],3)),
        ('Static margin / body width',f"{a['before']['minimum']['static_margin_body_widths']:.2f}",f"{a['after']['minimum']['static_margin_body_widths']:.2f}"),
        ('Sampled CP range',length(a['before']['minimum']['cp_x_mm'],3)+' to '+length(a['before']['maximum']['cp_x_mm'],3),length(a['after']['minimum']['cp_x_mm'],3)+' to '+length(a['after']['maximum']['cp_x_mm'],3)),
    ])
    text+='\nThe old cutout can already place its estimated CP behind its CG because the long pod/antenna has side area. That result does not establish enough restoring force near nose-down, a safe turn from level or adequate damping. The fins add deliberate surfaces in both steering planes; a positive area margin still does not demonstrate self-righting. The model starts at zero fall speed, when this aerodynamic moment is zero. Fin stall, changing pressure distribution, flexibility, pod wakes, angular inertia, propwash and gusts remain unknown. No turn time, minimum release height, upright landing or drop survival is claimed. The dummy drop test must establish the response.\n\n'
    text+=f"The hanger moves with the new mass solution to **{length(m['hanger_x_mm'],3)} from the tip**; its lateral axis follows the new CG. Four darts alone weigh **{mass(4*m['dart_total_g'])}**; four darts plus the unchanged harness weigh **{mass(m['carried_payload_g'])}**. The dummy is re-solved with the same fins, collars and adhesive to match the new mass and all three first moments; matching inertia and aerodynamic response is still approximate.\n\n"
    text+='**Keep flat carriage at the balance point.** A hanger slightly ahead of the CG, toward the point, would make the tail sag and the point rise. To start nose-down under gravity, the support must be slightly aft of the CG, toward the fins. Both signs were recomputed with the moved post mass rather than merely rotating the old drawing.\n\n'
    text+=table(['Hanger relative to CG','Gravity equilibrium, nose-down positive','Rigid head seating'],[
        ('Toward point by '+length(abs(c['hanger_offset_from_cg_mm']),3) if c['hanger_offset_from_cg_mm']<0 else 'At CG' if c['selected'] else 'Toward tail by '+length(c['hanger_offset_from_cg_mm'],3),
         f"{c['equilibrium_nose_down_deg']:.2f} degrees",'Clear' if not c['seating_collisions'] else 'Interferes with rotor/plate') for c in a['carriage']])
    text+='\nAn aft support could give an initial nose-down bias and shorten the required turn, but it lifts the long tail toward the aircraft, lowers the point toward the ground and puts the round head on an edge. The seating probe finds solid interference with the present horizontal support geometry, so the tilted alternatives are rejected before release qualification. Edge loading/wedging would also change extraction friction. Flat carriage preserves the full-head bearing surface and existing release path; its rotation must begin aerodynamically after release, with timing still unknown. Neither offset option is being advertised as a checked release configuration.\n\n'
    text+='### Wind estimate\n\nA finned dart tends to align with the air it falls through, which can incline its point into the wind rather than vertically. The requested no-drag arithmetic assumes release from rest, no horizontal ground speed, steady wind, vertical impact speed **sqrt(2 x gravity x height)** with **g = 32.174 ft/s²**, and perfect alignment. Tilt from vertical is **atan(wind / vertical impact speed)**.\n\n'
    text+=table(['Drop','No-drag impact speed','5 mph wind','10 mph wind','15 mph wind'],[(f"{r['drop_height_ft']:.0f} ft",f"{r['impact_speed_ft_s']:.1f} ft/s ({r['impact_speed_mph']:.1f} mph)",*[f"{r['tilt_deg'][str(w)]:.1f} degrees" for w in (5,10,15)]) for r in a['wind']])
    text+='\n**This is an estimate, not a test or a landing prediction.** Vertical drag lowers the impact speed and increases this tilt for an unchanged relative crosswind. Horizontal drag also accelerates the dart downwind and reduces the relative crosswind, which can reduce tilt; the net result needs coupled flight dynamics or measurements. Fin alignment may lag or oscillate and may not complete in a short drop. These numbers provide neither drift/aim accuracy nor permission to assume an upright impact. `dart_fall_sequence.png` shows illustrative attitudes only; pose spacing is neither time nor distance.\n\n'
    text+='Primary references for the qualitative CG/CP criterion and the simplified calculation are [NASA Glenn: generalized center of pressure](https://www1.grc.nasa.gov/beginners-guide-to-aeronautics/generalized-center-of-pressure/), [conditions for stability](https://www1.grc.nasa.gov/beginners-guide-to-aeronautics/conditions-for-rocket-stability/) and [falling objects with air resistance](https://www1.grc.nasa.gov/beginners-guide-to-aeronautics/falling-object-with-air-resistance/). Applying the cutout method to this irregular, initially horizontal dart is an engineering estimate, not validation by those references.\n\n'
    return text
